*** Add File:docs/runbooks/kms_rekor_and_detectors.md
+# Runbook — KMS, Rekor, ExternalSecrets and Production Detectors
+
+This document describes how to wire multiple KMS providers for cosign signing, configure Rekor, deploy ExternalSecrets and run production-grade moderation/PII/NLI services.
+
+1) KMS & cosign
+- The CI workflow (.github/workflows/cosign_kms_rekor_all.yml) accepts COSIGN_KMS_URI. Example URIs:
+  - AWS KMS: aws-kms://arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:123456789012:key/abcd-1234
+  - GCP KMS: gcp-kms://projects/<proj>/locations/global/keyRings/<ring>/cryptoKeys/<key>
+  - Azure Key Vault: azure-kv://https://<vault-name>.vault.azure.net/keys/<key>
+  - HashiCorp Vault (transit): vault://transit/<key-name>
+
+- Store COSIGN_KMS_URI and REKOR_SERVER in GitHub Secrets or provide via workflow dispatch.
+- The workflow will sign the given artifact using cosign and attempt to upload a Rekor entry (if REKOR_SERVER set).
+
+2) ExternalSecrets (SecretStore examples)
+- We provide SecretStore manifests for AWS SecretsManager, GCP Secret Manager, Azure Key Vault and Vault.
+- Deploy ExternalSecrets operator, then apply the appropriate SecretStore and ExternalSecret binds for MCP Postgres credentials.
+
+3) Production detectors (moderation / PII / NLI)
+- We provide dockerized services:
+  - moderation (Detoxify-backed): services/moderation/production
+  - pii (Presidio adapter): services/pii/presidio_adapter (requires a Presidio Analyzer deployment)
+  - verifier (NLI): services/verifier/nli
+- Use docker-compose.prod.yml for local integration testing, or build images and deploy via Helm/K8s.
+- Update LANGCHAIN runtime environment variables to point to these services:
+  - MODERATION_SVC (e.g. http://moderation:80)
+  - PII_SVC (e.g. http://pii:80)
+  - VERIFIER_SVC (e.g. http://verifier:80)
+
+4) Preflight behavior
+- The existing preflight implementation (langchain_runtime/preflight.py) already calls the endpoints above based on env vars. Ensure the runtime can reach these endpoints.
+
+5) Presidio
+- Presidio Analyzer & Recognizer are required for robust PII detection. See Microsoft Presidio docs and deploy analyzer + recognizer as separate services. The adapter calls PRESIDIO_ANALYZER env var endpoint.
+
+6) Rekor
+- Deploy Rekor (open-source) or use Sigstore/ Rekor hosted endpoint and set REKOR_SERVER. Ensure cosign uploading is allowed from your CI identity or that Rekor keys/policies are configured.
+
+7) IAM / Permissions
+- For each KMS provider, create a granular signing principal:
+  - AWS: create an IAM role allowing kms:Sign on the specific key; attach to the runner (OIDC / assume-role) or provide temporary credentials.
+  - GCP/Azure/Vault: follow provider-specific cosign KMS setup.
+
+8) Testing checklist
+- Sign a small artifact with COSIGN_KMS_URI via the CI workflow.
+- Verify that a .sig file is produced and Rekor reports an entry (if configured).
+- Start docker-compose.prod.yml and exercise moderation/PII/verifier endpoints with sample inputs.
+- Wire langchain_runtime to call run_preflight and validate end-to-end gating behavior.
+
